<h2>SEO and Google Business Profile</h2>
<p>Builders let you connect a domain, but canonical tags, redirect rules, and Search Console verification trip people up. On custom builds I configure GA4, Search Console, and call/form events under your login. GBP website field points to your domain, not a wixsite subdomain.</p>

<h2>When to stay on a builder</h2>
<p>You truly enjoy tweaking design yourself weekly. You sell only through Etsy or Amazon and need a link hub. Your franchise mandates a platform. You will not pay for custom until revenue justifies it — honest self-awareness.</p>

<h2>When to switch</h2>
<p>Renewal quote shocked you. Mobile PageSpeed scores stay red. You need booking tied to your calendar properly. You want print matched to web on Business Website tier. You are embarrassed to put the URL on your truck.</p>

<h2>Migration reality</h2>
<p>There is no magic import button. We reuse copy and images you own, rebuild information architecture, and 301 redirect old URLs when paths change. Expect a short SEO fluctuation week; rankings usually stabilize when content quality and NAP stay consistent.</p>

<h2>Security and maintenance</h2>
<p>Custom PHP sites on maintained hosting with Care Plans get backups and updates. Builders handle patches until they do not — and plugin equivalents on Wix still need attention. Either way, someone must watch SSL expiry.</p>

